Recognition of Prior Learning

People entering OCRA education may already hold relevant qualifications or substantial experience from obstacle sport or another discipline.

Where appropriate, OCRA may consider previous education and practical experience through Recognition of Prior Learning.

Recognition does not automatically remove all requirements.

Participants must still demonstrate the knowledge and standards required for the OCRA role or qualification they are seeking.


Continuing Development

Education does not end after completing a qualification.

OCRA will support continuing development through opportunities such as:

- Refresher courses
- Rules updates
- Workshops
- Specialist modules
- Mentoring
- Practical experience
- Advanced education

This helps coaches and Technical Officials remain current as the sport develops.


Interested in a Course?

If you are interested in coaching, Technical Officiating or another OCRA education opportunity and there is currently no suitable course listed, you can register your interest.

This will help OCRA understand demand and plan future education programmes.


